the right). A is fully negative, so it is not left-skewed. Therefore, neither lottery is left-skewed in the defined sense. The decision reason would prefer a lottery with more probability mass on favorable outcomes. Since both have only 0.1% favorable (B), and A has no favorable outcomes, B has more favorable probability mass. Thus, according to the reason, B should be preferred. The reason can be applied: the relevant information (probability mass on favorable vs. unfavorable outcomes) is present and can be derived from the lotteries.",
